<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-July trade surplus widens to $20.28 bln.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-July trade surplus widens to $20.28 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $20.3 billion in the first seven months of this year after a $18.6 billion surplus in the same period of 1995, the Ministry of Foreign Economic Relations said.</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE  Jan-July96  Jan-June96  Jan-July95</p>
<p>    exports			    38.85	 32.81	 37.37</p>
<p>    imports			    18.63	 15.47	 18.73</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +20.28	+17.33	+18.63</p>
<p>					  July 96	June 96     July 95</p>
<p>    exports			     6.04	  6.16	  4.98</p>
<p>    imports			     3.10	  2.46	  2.51</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +2.94	 +3.70	 +2.47</p>
<p>Notes - Figures in billion dollars, FOB. Differences due</p>
<p>rounding. Data are for trade with Russia's &quot;far abroad&quot;</p>
<p>excluding former Soviet states. Including trade with CIS</p>
<p>countries, the surplus in the first seven months widened to</p>
<p>$20.69 billion from $20.15 billion last year.</p>
<p>--Konstantin Kutsyllo, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
